# GCE UI Rules — Architecture 2.0 (permanent)

This is the **canonical Cursor UI governance rule**. It applies to:

1. Existing canonical GCE UI (Architecture 2.0 is the **migration target**)
2. **All future** GCE development that creates or materially changes UI — including later feature/PDF implementation — without the Founder repeating these instructions

Do not treat `docs/ui-ux/` as migration-only documentation.

## Authority (never invert)

```text
Founder Decisions / explicit Founder supersession
  → canonical Business Rules
  → Backend / State Machines / Security truth
  → Approved Feature Architecture (phase plans / ADRs)
  → GCE UI/UX Architecture 2.0          ← docs/ui-ux/
  → canonical Design System / frontend language
  → page / component implementation
```

UI/UX Architecture **must never** override higher-authority product, business, economic, security, or legal truth.

If a conflict is found: update the **lower-authority** artifact. Do not silently change higher-authority product behavior.

Visual tokens: `design-system/MASTER.md` + `lib/frontend/design-language.ts` + `lib/frontend/motion.ts`. MASTER wins on palette, type, radius, glass, dark surface.

Advisory only (cannot replace IA, shells, workspaces, or MASTER): ui-ux-pro-max, ui-styling, Taste, Impeccable, Emil, 21st.dev search-only. See `.cursor/rules/09_Design_Tooling_Governance.mdc`.

### Living Architecture 2.0 (read before UI work)

